/**
 * The Carbon -> lifekit colour bridge, as data. Carbon reads colour only through
 * `var(--cds-NAME, <fallback>)`, so pointing each semantic `--cds-*` name at one of our `--color-*`
 * roles makes every Carbon-specced value follow the app's seed palette and light/dark with no JS.
 * Our default look is Carbon's g10 shape (grey ground, white layer-01 and white fields), so the
 * mapping is close to one-to-one. `//` lines open a group in the generated file.
 *
 * Carbon's ten tag families fold onto our four status hues and neutral; cyan, teal, purple,
 * cool-gray and warm-gray tags keep Carbon's own colours until a decision is taken.
 * Names are the `--cds-` suffix; test/carbon-bridge.spec.mjs checks each is a real Carbon token
 * and that every `--color-*` role used here is defined in theme.css.
 */
